WEBVTT

00:00.890 --> 00:04.510
f is a linear function whose
table of values is shown below.

00:04.510 --> 00:06.540
And they give us three
different x-values

00:06.540 --> 00:08.980
and the corresponding
f of x values.

00:08.980 --> 00:13.210
Which graphs show functions that
are increasing faster than f?

00:13.210 --> 00:15.720
So when we're talking
about increasing faster,

00:15.720 --> 00:18.090
we're really talking
about a higher rate

00:18.090 --> 00:22.180
of change of y with respect to
f, or a higher rate of change

00:22.180 --> 00:24.380
of the vertical
axis with respect

00:24.380 --> 00:27.450
to the horizontal axis, which
is another way of saying which

00:27.450 --> 00:32.890
of these have a steeper
slope than the function f?

00:32.890 --> 00:36.150
So let's see what the
change in our vertical axis

00:36.150 --> 00:40.270
is with respect to our change
in our horizontal axis.

00:40.270 --> 00:44.550
Once again, the Greek
letter-- this triangle

00:44.550 --> 00:47.790
is the Greek letter delta, which
is shorthand for "change in."

00:47.790 --> 00:51.180
So this is the change in
f over the change in x.

00:51.180 --> 00:53.460
So we see over
here, when x changes

00:53.460 --> 00:59.930
by 1, the value of our
function changes by positive 5.

01:02.650 --> 01:05.310
And it's linear, so that's true.

01:05.310 --> 01:07.360
Between any two
points, the ratio

01:07.360 --> 01:10.410
between our change in f and
our change in x is the same.

01:10.410 --> 01:15.710
If we go up 1 again, we have
plus 1 in the x-direction,

01:15.710 --> 01:18.302
we are once again
increasing by 5.

01:18.302 --> 01:20.510
If you start from this point
and go all the way here,

01:20.510 --> 01:24.960
so if you go plus
2 along x, you're

01:24.960 --> 01:29.040
going to go plus 10 along f.

01:29.040 --> 01:31.590
So it would be 10 over
2, which is still 5.

01:31.590 --> 01:33.930
So either way, the
slope, or the rate

01:33.930 --> 01:36.090
of change of the vertical
axis with respect

01:36.090 --> 01:39.630
to the horizontal
axis, is 5 for f.

01:39.630 --> 01:42.790
Now, let's see which of
these increase faster.

01:42.790 --> 01:45.110
Well, a isn't even increasing.

01:45.110 --> 01:46.730
So A is decreasing.

01:46.730 --> 01:49.620
As x increases, y is decreasing.

01:49.620 --> 01:53.270
So that definitely
can't be the case.

01:53.270 --> 01:55.610
If we look at this
one right over here,

01:55.610 --> 01:59.790
it looks like-- let's see,
if we start over here,

01:59.790 --> 02:04.540
if we increase 1 along the
x-direction, if our change in x

02:04.540 --> 02:08.120
is 1, it looks like our
change in y is exactly 5-- 1,

02:08.120 --> 02:11.210
2, 3, 4, 5.

02:11.210 --> 02:16.410
So it looks like for choice
B, our slope is exactly

02:16.410 --> 02:19.940
5, or our change in y over
change in x is exactly 5.

02:19.940 --> 02:21.820
So it's not increasing
faster than f.

02:21.820 --> 02:24.060
It's increasing the same as f.

02:24.060 --> 02:26.040
Now let's look at
C. So I'm going

02:26.040 --> 02:29.494
to try to find a point where
it looks like I have an integer

02:29.494 --> 02:30.410
point right over here.

02:30.410 --> 02:33.610
So that's the point,
negative 3, negative 3.

02:33.610 --> 02:36.580
And if I move 1 in
the x-direction,

02:36.580 --> 02:38.980
it looks like I'm
increasing by more than 5.

02:38.980 --> 02:47.650
I'm increasing 1, 2, 3, 4,
5, 6, 7, 8, it looks like.

02:47.650 --> 02:51.320
So this one looks like
it has a slope of 8.

02:51.320 --> 02:55.110
So this one is
increasing faster than f,

02:55.110 --> 02:56.924
so we'll circle that
right over there.

02:56.924 --> 02:58.340
And now let's look
at this choice.

02:58.340 --> 03:00.370
So if we start right over here--
and I just picked this point

03:00.370 --> 03:02.500
because that's at a
nice integer coordinate.

03:02.500 --> 03:04.625
It's at the point 2, negative 4.

03:09.320 --> 03:13.310
If we increase x by 1,
then we increase y by 1,

03:13.310 --> 03:17.850
2, 3-- looks like about 3
and 1/2, definitely not 5.

03:17.850 --> 03:19.790
In order for it to
increase as fast as f,

03:19.790 --> 03:23.000
it would have to increase by 5,
so it would have to be up here.

03:23.000 --> 03:24.995
So it would have to
go 1, 2, 3, 4, 5.

03:24.995 --> 03:26.620
It would have had to
have been up here.

03:26.620 --> 03:30.990
The line would've looked
something more like that just

03:30.990 --> 03:34.030
to match f, much less
grow faster than f.

03:34.030 --> 03:36.230
So D does not meet the criteria.

03:36.230 --> 03:38.463
It is only C.
